IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `mda-types`

-- Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, Parts 2, 2A and 2B (ss 5 to 14, 8A, 11A to 11Q, 12 to 14), s 2 (the defined terms the offences turn on) and
-- ss 22A and 22B (proof of a psychoactive substance).
-- Source: source/MDA1973.txt lines 199 to 415 (s 2), 455 to 1432 (Parts 2, 2A, 2B), 1624 to 1664 (ss 22A, 22B).
--
-- The question this module answers: IS THIS AN OFFENCE UNDER THE ACT?  Part 2 (controlled drugs) and Part 2A (psychoactive substances, from 1 June
-- 2024) are mirror images: trafficking (5, 11F), manufacture (6, 11G), import and export (7, 11H), possession and consumption (8, 11I),
-- paraphernalia (9, 11K), premises (11, 11L), gatherings (11A, 11M), children and young persons (11B, 11N), introductions (11C, 11O), instruction
-- (11D, 11P) and young persons procured (11E, 11Q).  Each pair is one set of elements, tested against the kind of thing it is: a controlled drug (Part
-- 2) or a psychoactive substance (Part 2A).  A controlled drug is never a psychoactive substance (Fifth Schedule, para 4), so no thing engages both.
-- Presumptions (ss 17 to 22) and the punishments are in the other modules; here a presumed fact enters as a BOOLEAN input, as in the Prevention of
-- Corruption Act row's treatment of its section 8.

§ `2. Interpretation: controlled drug, psychoactive substance, excluded substance`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 2 'controlled drug'"
GIVEN s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a controlled drug` IF
    s's `the thing is specified in Part 1, 2 or 3 of the First Schedule, or is anything that contains a substance or product so specified`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 2 'controlled equipment, controlled material or controlled substance'"
GIVEN s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is controlled equipment, controlled material or a controlled substance` IF
    s's `the thing is specified in the Third Schedule`

-- "Excluded substance" is a substance specified in the Fifth Schedule, Part 1: alcohol, alkyl nitrites, chewing gum, ANY CONTROLLED DRUG OR
-- CONTROLLED SUBSTANCE (para 4), food, health product, herbal medicine, industrial material, intoxicating substance, medicinal product, poison, poppy
-- seed, psychotropic substance, a specified psychoactive substance of the Tobacco and Vaporisers Control Act 1993, a substance listed under the UN
-- conventions, tobacco, caffeine, nitrous oxide.  Paragraph 4 is the link to Part 2: it is derived from the other facts; the rest are one fact.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 2 'excluded substance'; Fifth Schedule, Part 1"
GIVEN s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is an excluded substance` IF
        `the thing is a controlled drug` s
    OR  `the thing is controlled equipment, controlled material or a controlled substance` s
    OR  s's `the thing is within a paragraph of Part 1 of the Fifth Schedule other than paragraph 4 (any controlled drug or controlled substance)`

-- "psychoactive substance": (a) a substance or product that has the capacity to have a psychoactive effect on an individual if the individual
-- smokes, administers to himself or herself or otherwise consumes it; but (b) does not include an excluded substance.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 2 'psychoactive substance'"
GIVEN s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is a psychoactive substance` IF
        s's `the thing has the capacity to have a psychoactive effect on an individual if the individual smokes, administers to himself or herself or otherwise consumes it`
    AND NOT `the thing is an excluded substance` s

-- 22A: in proceedings for the listed Part 2A offences, (a) to prove the thing is a psychoactive substance it is sufficient for the prosecution to
-- prove the capacity, and it is NOT necessary to prove that it is not an excluded substance; (b) a person who asserts that it is an excluded substance
-- bears the burden of proving that on a balance of probabilities.  So the prosecution's case on "psychoactive substance" is made by the capacity alone
-- unless the person asserts exclusion and proves it.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 22A"
GIVEN p IS A `Psychoactive Proof Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the thing is established as a psychoactive substance by section 22A` IF
        p's `the proceedings are for an offence under section 11F(1), 11G(1), 11H(1), 11I(1)(a) or (b), 11K(1), 11L(1), 11M(1), 11N(1) or (2), 11O(1), 11P(1) or (2) or 11Q(1)`
    AND p's `the prosecution proves that the thing has the capacity to have a psychoactive effect on an individual if the individual smokes, administers to himself or herself or otherwise consumes it`
    AND NOT (   p's `the person asserts that the thing is an excluded substance`
            AND p's `the person has proved on a balance of probabilities that the thing is an excluded substance`)

-- 22B: where knowledge that a substance is a psychoactive substance is a fault element, it is established if the person (a) knows that it has the
-- capacity to have a psychoactive effect and (b) did not believe or had no reason to believe that it is an excluded substance, "whether or not that
-- person knows the name or chemical composition of the psychoactive substance".  No fact about knowing the name is read.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 22B"
GIVEN p IS A `Psychoactive Proof Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `knowledge that the thing is a psychoactive substance is established by section 22B` IF
        p's `the person alleged to have committed the offence knows that the thing has the capacity to have a psychoactive effect`
    AND p's `the person alleged to have committed the offence did not believe, and had no reason to believe, that the thing is an excluded substance`

§ `5 and 11F. Trafficking`

-- "traffic" (s 2) means (a) to sell, give, administer, transport, send, deliver or distribute, or (b) to offer to do anything in (a), "otherwise than
-- under the authority of this Act".  5(1): except as authorised, an offence, on one's own behalf or another's, whether or not that other is in
-- Singapore, (a) to traffic, (b) to offer to traffic, or (c) to do or offer to do an act preparatory to or for the purpose of trafficking.  5(2): a
-- person commits the offence of trafficking if he has the drug in possession for the purpose of trafficking.  The third input is the outcome of the
-- section 17 presumption (mda-presumptions.l4), which stands for the possession-for-the-purpose element.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 2 'traffic', 5(1) and (2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Trafficking Facts`, `possession for the purpose of trafficking is presumed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused trafficked in the thing` IF
        NOT t's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND (   t's `the accused sold, gave, administered, transported, sent, delivered or distributed the thing`
         OR t's `the accused offered to sell, give, administer, transport, send, deliver or distribute the thing`
         OR t's `the accused did, or offered to do, an act preparatory to or for the purpose of trafficking in the thing`
         OR t's `the accused had the thing in his or her possession for the purpose of trafficking`
         OR `possession for the purpose of trafficking is presumed`)

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 5(1) and (2)"
GIVEN t IS A `Trafficking Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`, `possession for the purpose of trafficking is presumed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 5(1) is made out` IF
        `the accused trafficked in the thing` t `possession for the purpose of trafficking is presumed`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

-- 11F(6): a defence for the accused to prove, on a balance of probabilities, that he intended or believed that the psychoactive substance would be
-- used for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption, whether or not it is fit for human consumption.  11F(2), like 5(2), makes possession for
-- the purpose of trafficking the offence; there is no presumption of purpose in Part 2A (section 17 names controlled drugs only).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11F(1), (2) and (6)"
GIVEN t IS A `Trafficking Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`, l IS A `Legitimate Purpose Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11F(1) is made out` IF
        `the accused trafficked in the thing` t FALSE
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s
    AND NOT l's `the accused proves that the purpose was a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`

§ `6 and 11G. Manufacture`

-- "manufacture", in relation to a controlled drug, a controlled substance or a psychoactive substance, includes any process of producing it and the
-- refining or transformation of one into another.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 2 'manufacture', 6"
GIVEN m IS A `Manufacture Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 6 is made out` IF
        m's `the accused produced the thing, or refined it or transformed one thing into another`
    AND NOT m's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11G(1) and (3)"
GIVEN m IS A `Manufacture Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`, l IS A `Legitimate Purpose Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11G(1) is made out` IF
        m's `the accused produced the thing, or refined it or transformed one thing into another`
    AND NOT m's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s
    AND NOT l's `the accused proves that the purpose was a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`

§ `7 and 11H. Import and export`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 7"
GIVEN i IS AN `Import Export Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 7 is made out` IF
        i's `the accused imported the thing into Singapore or exported it from Singapore`
    AND NOT i's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11H(1) and (5)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Import Export Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`, l IS A `Legitimate Purpose Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11H(1) is made out` IF
        i's `the accused imported the thing into Singapore or exported it from Singapore`
    AND NOT i's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s
    AND NOT l's `the accused proves that the purpose was a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`

§ `8, 8A, 11I and 11J. Possession and consumption`

-- 8(a) possession; 8(b) to smoke, administer to himself or herself or otherwise consume (i) a controlled drug other than a specified drug, or (ii) a
-- specified drug (Fourth Schedule).  The punishment differs by (i) and (ii) only through section 33A, which is about specified drugs.  The first
-- input to 8(a) is the outcome of the section 18 presumption of possession.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 8(a)"
GIVEN c IS A `Possession Consumption Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`, `possession is presumed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8(a) is made out` IF
        (   c's `the accused had the thing in his or her possession`
         OR `possession is presumed`)
    AND NOT c's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 8(b)(i) and (ii)"
GIVEN c IS A `Possession Consumption Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8(b) is made out` IF
        c's `the accused smoked, administered to himself or herself or otherwise consumed the thing`
    AND NOT c's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 8(b)(ii); Fourth Schedule"
GIVEN c IS A `Possession Consumption Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 8(b)(ii) is made out` IF
        `an offence under section 8(b) is made out` c s
    AND c's `the controlled drug is a specified drug within the Fourth Schedule`

-- 8A: section 8(b) has effect in relation to a citizen of Singapore or a permanent resident of Singapore OUTSIDE as well as within Singapore, "where he
-- or she is found as a result of urine tests conducted under section 31(4)(b) to have" consumed the drug; where the offence is committed outside
-- Singapore he or she "may be dealt with as if that offence had been committed within Singapore".  11J is the same for 11I(1)(b).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, ss 8A(1) and (2), 11J(1) and (2)"
GIVEN o IS AN `Overseas Consumption Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the consumption outside Singapore may be dealt with as if it had been committed within Singapore` IF
        o's `the accused is a citizen of Singapore or a permanent resident of Singapore`
    AND o's `the accused was found as a result of urine tests conducted under section 31(4)(b) to have consumed the drug or substance`
    AND o's `the consumption took place outside Singapore`

-- 11I(1)(a) possession and (b) consumption of a psychoactive substance; 11I(4): a defence to (a) for the accused to prove a legitimate purpose other
-- than human consumption.  The first input to (a) is the outcome of the section 18A presumption of possession.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11I(1)(a) and (4)"
GIVEN c IS A `Possession Consumption Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`, `possession is presumed` IS A BOOLEAN, l IS A `Legitimate Purpose Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11I(1)(a) is made out` IF
        (   c's `the accused had the thing in his or her possession`
         OR `possession is presumed`)
    AND NOT c's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s
    AND NOT l's `the accused proves that the purpose was a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11I(1)(b)"
GIVEN c IS A `Possession Consumption Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11I(1)(b) is made out` IF
        c's `the accused smoked, administered to himself or herself or otherwise consumed the thing`
    AND NOT c's `the accused's act was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

§ `9 and 11K. Paraphernalia`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 9"
GIVEN p IS A `Paraphernalia Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 9 is made out` IF
        p's `the accused had in his or her possession a pipe, syringe, utensil, apparatus or other article`
    AND p's `the article was intended for the smoking, administration or consumption of the thing`
    AND NOT p's `the accused's possession was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11K(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Paraphernalia Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11K(1) is made out` IF
        p's `the accused had in his or her possession a pipe, syringe, utensil, apparatus or other article`
    AND p's `the article was intended for the smoking, administration or consumption of the thing`
    AND NOT p's `the accused's possession was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

§ `10. Cultivation`

-- 10 has no "except as authorised" clause.  The three plants: any plant of the genus Cannabis, the species papaver somniferum, or the genus
-- erythroxylon "from which cocaine can be extracted".
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 10"
GIVEN c IS A `Cultivation Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 10 is made out` IF
        c's `the accused cultivated a plant of the genus Cannabis`
    OR  c's `the accused cultivated a plant of the species papaver somniferum`
    OR  c's `the accused cultivated a plant of the genus erythroxylon from which cocaine can be extracted`

§ `10A. Equipment, materials or substances useful for manufacture`

-- 10A(1): manufactures, supplies, possesses, or imports or exports controlled equipment, material or substance "knowing or having reason to believe"
-- that it is to be used in or for the manufacture of a controlled drug in contravention of section 6.  10A(2): it is no defence to the import or export
-- limb that the equipment, material or substance is the subject of a licence, permit or other authorisation under regulations made under section 10B.
-- The licence field is therefore read for nothing, and is a field so a test can show it.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 10A(1) and (2)"
GIVEN c IS A `Controlled Equipment Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 10A is made out` IF
        (   c's `the accused manufactured controlled equipment, controlled material or a controlled substance`
         OR c's `the accused supplied it to another person`
         OR c's `the accused had it in his or her possession`
         OR c's `the accused imported it or exported it`)
    AND c's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that it was to be used in or for the manufacture of a controlled drug in contravention of section 6`

§ `11 and 11L. Responsibilities of owners, tenants, etc.`

-- 11: the owner, tenant, occupier or person in charge of any place or premises who PERMITS OR SUFFERS it to be opened, kept or used for (a) the
-- purpose of smoking, administration or consumption of a controlled drug in contravention of section 8(b) or (b) the unlawful trafficking in or the
-- unlawful manufacturing of a controlled drug.  11L: "permit or allow", for a psychoactive substance.  "Place" includes a vessel, aircraft, train or vehicle.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11"
GIVEN p IS A `Premises Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11 is made out` IF
        p's `the accused was the owner, tenant, occupier or person in charge of the place or premises`
    AND (   p's `the accused permitted, suffered or allowed the place or premises or part of it to be opened, kept or used for smoking, administration or consumption of the thing in contravention of section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b)`
         OR p's `the accused permitted, suffered or allowed the place or premises or part of it to be opened, kept or used for the unlawful trafficking in or the unlawful manufacturing of the thing`)
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11L(1)"
GIVEN p IS A `Premises Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11L(1) is made out` IF
        p's `the accused was the owner, tenant, occupier or person in charge of the place or premises`
    AND (   p's `the accused permitted, suffered or allowed the place or premises or part of it to be opened, kept or used for smoking, administration or consumption of the thing in contravention of section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b)`
         OR p's `the accused permitted, suffered or allowed the place or premises or part of it to be opened, kept or used for the unlawful trafficking in or the unlawful manufacturing of the thing`)
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

§ `11A and 11M. Arranging or planning gatherings`

-- "Where there is a gathering of 2 or more persons in any place, any person who arranges or plans the gathering with the knowledge that" the drug is,
-- or is to be, consumed (in contravention) or trafficked at it.  11A(2), 11M(4): the person may be guilty "even though he or she does not supply" any.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11A(1) and (2)"
GIVEN g IS A `Gathering Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11A is made out` IF
        g's `there was a gathering of 2 or more persons in a place`
    AND g's `the accused arranged or planned the gathering`
    AND g's `the accused knew that the thing was, or was to be, consumed in contravention of section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b), or unlawfully trafficked, at the gathering`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11M(1) and (4)"
GIVEN g IS A `Gathering Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11M(1) is made out` IF
        g's `there was a gathering of 2 or more persons in a place`
    AND g's `the accused arranged or planned the gathering`
    AND g's `the accused knew that the thing was, or was to be, consumed in contravention of section 8(b) or 11I(1)(b), or unlawfully trafficked, at the gathering`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

§ `11B and 11N. Exposing a child; permitting a young person to consume`

-- 11B(1): a person 21 or older who, in possession of a controlled drug or drug paraphernalia, (a) knowingly or recklessly leaves it exposed in a place or in
-- a refrigerator, cupboard, cabinet, box, chest or other article that is not locked, and (b) knows that a child (below 16) has or is likely to have access.
-- 11B(2): a person 21 or older who, in possession of a controlled drug, (a) permits a young person (below 21) to smoke, administer or consume it, or (b)
-- does not take all reasonable steps to prevent it.  11B(4): (1) does not apply where the possession is authorised under the Act.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11B(1), (4) and (5)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exposure Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11B(1) is made out` IF
        e's `the accused is 21 years of age or older`
    AND e's `the accused was in possession of the thing or of drug paraphernalia`
    AND e's `the accused knowingly or recklessly left it exposed in a place, or in a refrigerator, cupboard, cabinet, box, chest or other article that is not locked`
    AND e's `the accused knew that a child below 16 years of age has, or is likely to have, access to the place or article`
    AND NOT e's `the accused's possession was authorised under this Act`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11B(2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exposure Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11B(2) is made out` IF
        e's `the accused is 21 years of age or older`
    AND e's `the accused was in possession of the thing or of drug paraphernalia`
    AND (   e's `the accused permitted a young person to smoke, administer or consume the thing`
         OR e's `the accused did not take all reasonable steps to prevent a young person from smoking, administering or consuming the thing`)
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

-- 11N(5): (1) does not apply to authorised possession.  11N(6): in proceedings for (1) in relation to possession of a psychoactive substance, it is a
-- defence for the accused to prove a legitimate purpose other than human consumption.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11N(1), (5), (6) and (7)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exposure Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11N(1) is made out` IF
        e's `the accused is 21 years of age or older`
    AND e's `the accused was in possession of the thing or of drug paraphernalia`
    AND e's `the accused knowingly or recklessly left it exposed in a place, or in a refrigerator, cupboard, cabinet, box, chest or other article that is not locked`
    AND e's `the accused knew that a child below 16 years of age has, or is likely to have, access to the place or article`
    AND NOT e's `the accused's possession was authorised under this Act`
    AND NOT e's `the accused proves that he or she had the psychoactive substance in his or her possession for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11N(2)"
GIVEN e IS AN `Exposure Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11N(2) is made out` IF
        e's `the accused is 21 years of age or older`
    AND e's `the accused was in possession of the thing or of drug paraphernalia`
    AND (   e's `the accused permitted a young person to smoke, administer or consume the thing`
         OR e's `the accused did not take all reasonable steps to prevent a young person from smoking, administering or consuming the thing`)
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

§ `11C and 11O. Introducing a drug trafficker to another person`

-- 11C(1): A, knowing or having reason to believe (a) that B intends to procure a controlled drug whose possession by B would not be authorised, or (b)
-- that B intends, without authorisation, to smoke, administer or consume a controlled drug, introduces B to a person whom A knows or has reason to
-- believe is trafficking in a controlled drug and is likely to supply B.  "Introduce" includes giving an address, telephone number, email address or other
-- details.  11C(3): it is not necessary to prove that B in fact procures or consumes, or that both are in Singapore.  11O(5): a defence to 11O(1)(a) for
-- the accused to prove that he or she believed that B intended to procure the psychoactive substance for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11C(1), (3) and (4)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Introduction Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11C(1) is made out` IF
        (   i's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that another person intends to procure the thing, and that his or her possession of it would not be authorised`
         OR i's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that another person intends, without authorisation, to smoke, administer or consume the thing`)
    AND i's `the accused introduced that person to a person whom the accused knows or has reason to believe is trafficking in the thing and is likely to supply it`
    AND `the thing is a controlled drug` s

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11O(1), (4), (5) and (6)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Introduction Facts`, s IS A `Substance Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11O(1) is made out` IF
        (   (   i's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that another person intends to procure the thing, and that his or her possession of it would not be authorised`
            AND NOT i's `the accused proves that he or she believed that the other person intended to procure the psychoactive substance for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`)
         OR i's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that another person intends, without authorisation, to smoke, administer or consume the thing`)
    AND i's `the accused introduced that person to a person whom the accused knows or has reason to believe is trafficking in the thing and is likely to supply it`
    AND `the thing is a psychoactive substance` s

§ `11D and 11P. Instructing; disseminating information`

-- 11D(1): a person who teaches or instructs another (or provides information) to carry out cultivating cannabis, opium poppy or coca, manufacturing,
-- consuming, trafficking or doing an act preparatory, or importing or exporting, "knowing or having reason to believe that B intends to carry out the
-- activity".  11D(6): not applicable where authorised under the Act.  11D(7): a defence to prove a legitimate purpose related to the administration of
-- justice, the investigation and prosecution of offences, or science, medicine, education or art.  11D(2): disseminating or publishing information on
-- the activities; 11D(8) authorised; 11D(9) the same defence as 11D(7).  11P adds (9)(b) and (c): a defence of believing that B intended to manufacture
-- or to traffic, import or export for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption, which the encoding applies to every activity other than the
-- activity of consuming alone (fork F9 in NOTES.md).
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11D(1), (5), (6) and (7)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Instruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11D(1) is made out` IF
        i's `the accused taught or instructed another person to carry out, or provided him or her with information on carrying out, an activity mentioned in section 11D(1) or 11P(1)`
    AND i's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that the other person intended to carry out the activity`
    AND NOT i's `the teaching, instruction, provision, dissemination or publication was authorised under this Act`
    AND NOT i's `the accused proves that it had a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice, the investigation and prosecution of offences, or to science, medicine, education or art`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11D(2), (8) and (9)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Instruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11D(2) is made out` IF
        i's `the accused disseminated or published, or caused the dissemination or publication of, information on carrying out such an activity`
    AND NOT i's `the teaching, instruction, provision, dissemination or publication was authorised under this Act`
    AND NOT i's `the accused proves that it had a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice, the investigation and prosecution of offences, or to science, medicine, education or art`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11P(1), (7), (8) and (9)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Instruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11P(1) is made out` IF
        i's `the accused taught or instructed another person to carry out, or provided him or her with information on carrying out, an activity mentioned in section 11D(1) or 11P(1)`
    AND i's `the accused knew or had reason to believe that the other person intended to carry out the activity`
    AND NOT i's `the teaching, instruction, provision, dissemination or publication was authorised under this Act`
    AND NOT i's `the accused proves that it had a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice, the investigation and prosecution of offences, or to science, medicine, education or art`
    AND NOT (   i's `the accused proves that he or she believed that the activity was for a legitimate purpose other than human consumption`
            AND NOT i's `the activity is only smoking, administering or consuming a psychoactive substance, and not manufacture, trafficking, importing or exporting`)

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11P(2), (10) and (11)"
GIVEN i IS AN `Instruction Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11P(2) is made out` IF
        i's `the accused disseminated or published, or caused the dissemination or publication of, information on carrying out such an activity`
    AND NOT i's `the teaching, instruction, provision, dissemination or publication was authorised under this Act`
    AND NOT i's `the accused proves that it had a legitimate purpose related to the administration of justice, the investigation and prosecution of offences, or to science, medicine, education or art`

§ `11E and 11Q. Causing or procuring a young person or vulnerable person to commit certain offences`

-- 11E: a person of or above 21 who causes or procures a young person (below 21) or a vulnerable person to commit an offence under section 5(1) or 7.
-- 11Q: the same for an offence under 11F(1) or 11H(1).  The input says whether the young or vulnerable person committed the named offence.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11E"
GIVEN y IS A `Young Person Facts`, `the young person or vulnerable person committed an offence under section 5(1) or 7` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11E is made out` IF
        y's `the accused is 21 years of age or older`
    AND y's `the accused caused or procured a young person or a vulnerable person to commit the offence`
    AND `the young person or vulnerable person committed an offence under section 5(1) or 7`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 11Q(1)"
GIVEN y IS A `Young Person Facts`, `the young person or vulnerable person committed an offence under section 11F(1) or 11H(1)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `an offence under section 11Q(1) is made out` IF
        y's `the accused is 21 years of age or older`
    AND y's `the accused caused or procured a young person or a vulnerable person to commit the offence`
    AND `the young person or vulnerable person committed an offence under section 11F(1) or 11H(1)`

§ `12, 13, 14. Abetment, attempts, preparatory acts; offences abroad; body corporate`

-- 12: "Any person who abets the commission of or who attempts to commit or does any act preparatory to, or in furtherance of, the commission of any
-- offence under this Act shall be guilty of that offence and shall be liable on conviction to the punishment provided for that offence."  The abetting,
-- attempting or preparatory act is the offence and has the same punishment: in the Second Schedule's rows by the offence's own section.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 12"
GIVEN s IS A `Secondary Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is guilty of the offence by section 12` IF
        s's `the accused abetted the commission of an offence under this Act`
    OR  s's `the accused attempted to commit an offence under this Act`
    OR  s's `the accused did an act preparatory to, or in furtherance of, the commission of an offence under this Act`

-- 13: a person who (a) aids, abets, counsels or procures the commission in a place outside Singapore of an offence punishable under a corresponding law
-- there, (b) aids, abets, counsels or procures the commission of an offence under the Act within Singapore even though the acts were done outside
-- Singapore, or (c) does an act preparatory to or in furtherance of an act outside Singapore which if committed in Singapore would constitute an
-- offence under the Act, is guilty: for (a) and (c) 2 to 10 years or a fine of $4,000 to $40,000 or both; for (b) the same punishment as the offence aided.
@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 13(a), (b) and (c)"
GIVEN s IS A `Secondary Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is guilty of an offence under section 13(a) or (c)` IF
        s's `the accused aided, abetted, counselled or procured the commission, in a place outside Singapore, of an offence punishable under a corresponding law in force in that place`
    OR  s's `the accused did an act preparatory to, or in furtherance of, an act outside Singapore which if committed in Singapore would constitute an offence under this Act`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 13(b)"
GIVEN s IS A `Secondary Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the accused is guilty of an offence under section 13(b)` IF
    s's `the accused aided, abetted, counselled or procured the commission of an offence under this Act within Singapore, even though all or any of the acts were done outside Singapore`

@ref "Misuse of Drugs Act 1973, s 14"
GIVEN s IS A `Secondary Liability Facts`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the officer of the body corporate is guilty as well as the body corporate` IF
    s's `the offence was committed by a body corporate with the consent or connivance of, or was attributable to any neglect on the part of, the accused as a director, manager, secretary or similar officer, or a person purporting to act as one`
